ret e
end
# The end of a chunk (see `wachunk`): the state p0 after the p1 functions of the chunk (first
# function p3, iteration bounds p2, variant count p4 before the chunk): the trailer, or the
# requested bodies, and the result code. compiler/boot.a0 runs the same fold with its own body
# (`wxfunf`, which emits a function from its fused form when loop fusion applies)
fn wachunkend (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32) u32 u32x128x8 u32 u32 -> (io,u32)
b mov p1
e mov p0
f at e 0
g at e 1
h at e 2
i at e 3
j at e 4
k at e 5
l gt i 0
m select l false true
n gt k 0
o select n false true
p and m o
q select p 1 0
r select l 1 0
s select l i 0
t select p b 0
u fold wxwq s f j
v fold wawr r u i
w fold watrail t v h p2 p3
x sub g p4
y fold wawr q w x
z fold wawr q y b
aa eq k 1
ab select aa 4 5
ac select n ab 0
ad select l 7 ac
ae rec z ad
ret ae
end
# The chunk: functions [p12, p13) of the checked tables (p1 types, p2 tlist, p3 fns, p4 nodes, p5
# operands, p6 node types, p7 name bytes, p8 fnm, p9 the call table (given for the functions
# before p12), p10 the iteration bounds, p11 the type count, p14 the variant count before the
# chunk, p15 the shape table, p16 p17 the simd and unroll options). Writes the records of
# `wxfun`, then (index, depth, bound) of each function, the chunk's variant count and its
# function count; or, when a body is missing (code 7), the chunk functions wanted and their count;
# or code 4 (a capacity) / 5 (an unsupported shape)
fn wachunk io u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x132 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x128x400 u32x128x16 u32x128x16 u32x128x8 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x200 u32 u32 -> (io,u32)
a call wainfo p1 p2 p11
b sub p13 p12
c call z8
d rec p0 p14 p9 0 c 0
e fold wxfun b d p12 p16 p17 p3 p4 p5 p6 p1 p2 a p15 p7 p8
r call wachunkend e b p10 p12 p14
ret r
end
